# Verify skills, feature maps, and behaviour checks (docs/guide/how-verify-maps.md).
title: A failed behaviour check blocks the gate at once, map drift is a warning until a dated config value, and an agent app the user installed fixes the map in its own pull request
direction: down
run: Pull request in the merge gate, or the nightly sweep
map: feature-map floor: compare each map with the source
sel: Pick checks: touched features and mapped criteria
ctl: Control tool in the product's stack runs each check
res: passed, failed, or unreachable, with artifacts
gate: A failed check fails the floor: gate red
drift: Drift: advisory until drift_blocking_from
brief: verify --maintain posts the brief on one issue
app: Agent app opens at most one map pull request
red: Bug story: proving tests rerun on the base commit
run -> map
run -> sel
run -> red: type:bug story
sel -> ctl: check JSON on stdin
ctl -> res: result JSON on stdout
res -> gate: any failed
map -> drift: drift found
drift -> brief: sweep or weekly loop
brief -> app
